{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/900909-have-you-ever-used-the-werewolf-trinity-in-your-mage-game","id":900909,"title":"Have you ever used the Werewolf Trinity in your mage game?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-05-27T06:54:18-07:00","id":900909,"title":"Have you ever used the Werewolf Trinity in your mage game?","content":"If so, what happened? All imaginable sorts of werewolf crossover, perhaps?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4173-numinous","name":"Numinous","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T09:10:08-07:00","id":901051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Numinous</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/900909-have-you-ever-used-the-werewolf-trinity-in-your-mage-game#post900909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If so, what happened? All imaginable sorts of werewolf crossover, perhaps?</div> </div> </div> </div>What do you mean? Do you mean did Pattern Spiders ever show up? Or do you mean the NWO is run by drider-like human mage/Pattern Spider amalgams? Do you mean a fomori or Bane makes an apperance? Or fighting that the cabal is consumed fighting a Pentex with a heavy crossover with Technephandi?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T09:44:26-07:00","id":901085,"title":"","content":"Or Dynamic, Entropic, and Static Essence?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T10:00:00-07:00","id":901101,"title":"","content":"I dislike that cosmic trinity, for me the true order isn't frozen but dinamic, because armony is flexible, To create you need discipline, self control, effort and hard work, you need the order to change the things. They are in my setting, and they are powerful like kings or president of a multitational company, but they aren't like supreme deities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Tell me what you brag and I will tell you what you lack&quot; (Spanish saying)<br /> <br /> \u00abThe Master Confucius said: \u201cThe noble man is in harmony but does not follow the crowd. The inferior man follows the crowd, but is not in harmony\u201d\u00bb (Anaclet 13:23)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11152-luis-carlos","name":"Luis Carlos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"258"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T10:27:56-07:00","id":901133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Luis Carlos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/900909-have-you-ever-used-the-werewolf-trinity-in-your-mage-game?p=901101#post901101\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">because armony is flexible</div> </div> </div> </div>Harmony is a mix of all three.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T03:35:31-07:00","id":901925,"title":"","content":"It causes a lot of headaches, especially when it comes to interacting with spirits. Various paradigms see the spirit world differently and interact only with spirits from certain areas. This can cause a lot toes to get stepped on","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T06:37:07-07:00","id":901994,"title":"","content":"You need Mages that would end up into the Middle Umbra, and it's related Videre, when they stepp sideways. Otherwise they may end up in different places, or seeing different things in the same place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T07:58:12-07:00","id":902048,"title":"","content":"Generally I'm with Aleph, Werewolf cosmology is a Middle Umbral thing, most mages deal with the High Umbra.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T09:55:57-07:00","id":902114,"title":"","content":"Committing to an actual answer: Yes. I have used it obliquely, sparingly and with a very light touch. It also depended entirely on the character of the Mage chronicle in question. I remember having a character see a Pattern Spider using its webbing to bind and compress together natural spirits into a highway. That was a LONG time ago. Sometime in the mid-90s. That's probably the strongest direct connection, though cabals have fought a Black Spiral Dancer Theurge and his Banes at one point in the midst of very badly maintained oil refinery. Was the Wyrm or Weaver ever mentioned? No. Were the trappings used? Sure. However, I have run entire games where a LOT occurred in the Umbrae and the Triat were conspicuous by their complete absence. <br /> <br /> However, though the High Umbra gets mentioned incessantly as being the &quot;most mage-ly&quot; of the Umbrae, it's never been used much in any of my games. Most of the characters who have heavily invested in Spirit are the kind of casters who don't give a fig for talking to the English language or discussing philosophies of the color Blue. They tend to be shamanic types and the Vidare has been the Middle Umbra. Followed by those who cared a great deal about talking to the dead and messing with the Low/Dark Umbra. With a heavy dose of whatever Umbra Conventional Space and Etherspace belong to. Though the High Umbra gets a lot of press, the mages who are the most directly involved with Spirit (e.g. Dreamspeakers) are those that are seen as being intrinsically tied to the Middle, not High Umbra. (Sure there are SOME Dreamspeakers that tend towards the High or Low Umbrae, but a lot of flavor text bends against that.) EVERY Dreamspeaker in EVERY Mage game I've run has had a lot of Spirit. A few of the Order of Hermes mages and Choristers have had it to summon angels and gnostic archetypes. <br /> <br /> So, I guess, the Triat is actually something of a thing to deal with, as a lot of the detailing of the Middle Umbra started in Werewolf and is still characterized by that basis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T13:19:23-07:00","id":902255,"title":"","content":"The High Umbra is where you find Ether space. its where you as an Etherite can throw it in the face of all those dirty hippies that Asgard is a place of grand Kirby Science! That is to say.. its a matter of perspective. Chorusters and Hermetics go to meet angels. Etherites go to meet ancient Aliens, and Verbena talk to Gods. And then they yell at eachother for getting it all wrong","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T13:58:42-07:00","id":902274,"title":"","content":"Honestly, after having played on a crossover Mush for a while, Werewolf and Mage really don't play nicely with one another, despite a superficial similarity.<br /> <br /> Werewolf is about an apocalypse, and it's world is built accordingly. If you try to lay it side by side with Mage it kind of makes that apocalypse moot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T16:58:53-07:00","id":902372,"title":"","content":"I've never run a Mage game, but I've always run my chronicles with the assumption that Mages know better than the others how the universe really works, and that the whole World of Darkness really follows its precepts. (Wraith deal with very existential/metaphysical issues as well, and some Gaunts may know more about the nature of Oblivion and the Neverborn better than Mages). So anything that happens in the other games I run, is done with that mindset. So even though I generally only run Vampire and Werewolf, I do it with Mage in mind. This has never been apparent to the players though.<br /> <br /> As such, I hold that the Wyld, Weaver, and the Wyrm are mere anthropomorphized understandings/caricature of the Mage paradigm of Dynamism, Stasis, and Entropy. The Garou may understand many things and details about the spirit world more than Mages, but they are actually quite weak on major metaphysical philosophies. Attributing all their problems to the Wyrm is simply their way of dealing with the Problem of Evil.<br /> <br /> The game was originally written with the intent that all of them crossovered to one another. That quickly fell apart as 1) there were not enough common mechanics to make it work, 2) as each line developed, little bits of inconsistent canon were introduced especially as the first games had many more supplements published before some of the game lines had even begun, and 3) the various line developers became very protective of their own line and couldn't work well with others to tell a single setting. There were too many ideas (and egos) that worked against each other. So before too long, the line changed from crossover is great and allowed, to none of the games crossover and canon in one game shouldn't be taken into the next line. That way each developer could do whatever they liked and ignore what another developer was doing. Well, it is at least one way of dealing with office politics.<br /> <br /> But before that happened, to me it was very clear that Dynamism, Stasis, and Entropy was the basis for Wyld, Weaver, and the Wyrm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T10:32:00-07:00","id":903642,"title":"","content":"I do not use it directly. I tend to think the Werewolf trinity is a narrowed concept of the metaphysical trinity. The last one, even if not named that way in all paradigms (and therefore in all Traditions) is present in all beliefs. Some Choristers will speak about the different faces of the One, other Dreamspeakers will speak about the greater spirits entities and most Hermetic will directly recognize the metaphysical trinity.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure Mages do know better than others, but they surely think they do. In my opinion, the Wyld, the Weaver and the Wyrm are part of Dynamism, Stasis and Entropy. May be they even exist as spiritual beings. Since the metaphysical trinity is built on concepts, spiritual representations of these concepts should exist. In my WoD, the Werewolf trinity is formed of these representations. However, this is a personal interpretation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8572-nicotheduck","name":"NicoTheDuck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T11:27:47-07:00","id":903675,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/900909-have-you-ever-used-the-werewolf-trinity-in-your-mage-game?p=901925#post901925\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It causes a lot of headaches, especially when it comes to interacting with spirits. Various paradigms see the spirit world differently and interact only with spirits from certain areas. This can cause a lot toes to get stepped on</div> </div> </div> </div>I've run into this particular problem several times playing Hermetics and Etherites interacting with spirits run by STs that conceive of them pretty much solely from a Werewolf perspective. WtA has the most robust rules for dealing with spirits, and players are often acquainted with multiple game lines so its an understandable bias, but it causes problems when someone tells you that spirits won't respond to your invocation because &quot;they don't work like that.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T09:48:40-07:00","id":905023,"title":"","content":"(I shouldn't be jumping in on this, as I have a shit-ton of stuff to do... but a friend linked this topic to me with a <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> because of how long this type of discussion has gone on across the various forums... and because of the strange -- almost bizarre -- cognitive dissonance that seems to affect a number of people concerning this &quot;cross-over&quot;...)<br /> <br /> The Weaver, Wyld and Wyrm are simply the Garou/Fera perceptions and manifestations of Stasis, Dynamism and Entropic aspects in the (broader-ranging) Mage (C)osmology. The 3-Ws are simply the (mostly) Middle-Umbra manifestation of the more broad/permeating aspects of SDE (in whatever order) in Mage (not only in the High Umbra, as some misattribute, but also in the Deep/Far and Low Umbrae, as well).<br /> <br /> It creates absolutely *no conflict* whatsoever, save for in the minds of those who don't quite &quot;get&quot; how different things appear differently to different beings/entities as well as manifest in somewhat different ways along the different levels (and reaches) of the various Umbrae of WoD cosmology.<br /> <br /> (Now, *in-narratively*, there can be centuries-to-millennia-long debates/arguments between various mage and garou *characters* as to how &quot;x,y and z&quot; are this, that and the other... but *meta-narratively*, there should be absolutely no issue whatsoever in crossing over the 3-W aspects into a Mage setting. Hell, for a number of Dreamspeakers as well as more than a few Verbena, the 3-W are something they'd likely have learned about and/or interacted with during various excursions into the Middle Umbra; they might refer to these &quot;entities&quot; by somewhat different names and/or conceptualizations -- particularly in the case of especially erudite/aware Mages, who may have a broader perspective/insight into the universe as a whole than most Garou/Fera would or do -- but by-and-large they'd be just as aware of the Middle Umbra &quot;identities&quot; of Stasis(Weaver), Dynamism(Wyld) and Entropy(Wyrm) as most were-creatures, particularly in the case of the aforementioned Dreamspeakers, save again for having different names and/or metaphysical perspectives...)<br /> <br /> It's really no big deal at all. Like, <i>at all</i>...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have been around here for waaaayyyy too fucking long...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","name":"Just John, Forever...","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T13:38:47-07:00","id":905146,"title":"","content":"The issue is not that 'it looks different' it's that quite a few of the metaphysics of Werewolf basically make no sense whatsoever from the point of view of mage. A Matter 2/ Correspondence 2/Spirit 2 Effect could potentially kill one of the biggest bads of the Werewolf setting with zero chance for that big bad to fight back. The entire setting has a sort of 'this is really hard for WEREWOLVES to do but absolutely trivial for a mage to do.' problem to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T15:41:23-07:00","id":905225,"title":"","content":"Really?, How it's so?. What kind of effect and why it shouldn't be possible to counter using some spiritual reality warping stuff?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T18:11:00-07:00","id":905296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/900909-have-you-ever-used-the-werewolf-trinity-in-your-mage-game?p=905225#post905225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really?, How it's so?. What kind of effect and why it shouldn't be possible to counter using some spiritual reality warping stuff?</div> </div> </div> </div>Lord Steel. Break the mask. Seal him into a mirrored bubble. For extra fun, banish that mirror bubble from space and time so it can never be found again. Screwing over any attempts to free him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T18:54:40-07:00","id":905318,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/900909-have-you-ever-used-the-werewolf-trinity-in-your-mage-game?p=905296#post905296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Lord Steel. Break the mask. Seal him into a mirrored bubble. For extra fun, banish that mirror bubble from space and time so it can never be found again. Screwing over any attempts to free him.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because Mage crossover obviously wouldn't invite other mages to go and undo your spell, ruining your clever plan. Assuming that it works on a Maeljin in the first place, since, as Incarnae, they don't have stats.<br /> <br /> Edit: Said with less snark, generally, crossover tends to result in no net gain of anything, since you end up having to deal with the game's antagonists, who have the same capabilities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":". 06-01-2016, 10:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T18:57:19-07:00","id":905320,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/900909-have-you-ever-used-the-werewolf-trinity-in-your-mage-game?p=905296#post905296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Lord Steel. Break the mask. Seal him into a mirrored bubble. For extra fun, banish that mirror bubble from space and time so it can never be found again. Screwing over any attempts to free him.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you do this before or after you quantify the number of angels that can dance on the head of a pin?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T19:13:11-07:00","id":905329,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lord Steel. Break the mask. Seal him into a mirrored bubble. For extra fun, banish that mirror bubble from space and time so it can never be found again. Screwing over any attempts to free him.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can't seal a spirit into a physical object with Spirit 2, you need Spirit 4 for that.<br /> With 2 you can only increase the local Gauntlet, and trap spirits within it, but it isn't an invulnerable seal (anything that can pierce the Gauntlet can pierce your trap, as it's made with the Gauntlet itself).<br /> <br /> And you always forget the most important part, the difficulty:<br /> <br /> The entrapping of a spirit needs a number of successes appropiate for the power of the Spirit. This depends, partly, on the judgement of the Storyteller, but you shouldn't assume that entrapping an Incarna will be easier than impossible (I wouldn't allow it with less than 100 successes, being very generous. All the Council of Nine was needed to entrap a single Incarna in the foundation of Horizon, it's not easy).<br /> As you can see, the system bends arround these &quot;perceived issues&quot; quite easily. Once again, I need to remember to you that magick it's deffined by its difficulty, not only by the Spheres, and entrapping an Incarna it's easily &gt;= &quot;Godlike Feat&quot;<br /> <br /> Plus, you may not know this but, in Mage, powerful spirits have Mage Spheres as a representation of their vast and all encompassing power. This it's a rule that existed from the first edition to the last. Since Lord Steel hasn't character sheet, what makes you think that he shouldn't have &quot;Spheres&quot;?. Since in werewolf these spirits can do &quot;anything within their purview&quot;, it seems appropiate that they can use open ended powers affectin all layers of reality within the conjceptual domain of the spirit. Meaning that the spirit can probably release itself or merely counter your powers with his own Dynamic Magick(tm).<br /> <br /> And that's without even entering in &quot;Storyteller's Fiat Realm&quot;. And Incarnae live in that Realm, ask any Mage book about Spirits, from the Book of Madness to M20.They all will say the same: These entities can't be faced directly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 06-01-2016, 10:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T02:19:21-07:00","id":905489,"title":"","content":"It is a big deal thematically. If you're playing Mage with Werewolf elements, you're fine. If you try to do it on a level where they are equals or vice versa... it's going to fall apart.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T10:36:04-07:00","id":906539,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/900909-have-you-ever-used-the-werewolf-trinity-in-your-mage-game?p=905318#post905318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Because Mage crossover obviously wouldn't invite other mages to go and undo your spell, ruining your clever plan. Assuming that it works on a Maeljin in the first place, since, as Incarnae, they don't have stats.<br /> <br /> Edit: Said with less snark, generally, crossover tends to result in no net gain of anything, since you end up having to deal with the game's antagonists, who have the same capabilities.</div> </div> </div> </div>Assuming of course that for whatever reasons, the crossover ends up with neatly arranged sides of equivalent power.<br /> <br /> When there's no reason for this to occur, because Werewolves are kind of at best inept luddites, and at worst hidebound sociopathic morons who ruin almost everything they are tasked with...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/900909-have-you-ever-used-the-werewolf-trinity-in-your-mage-game?p=905320#post905320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Do you do this before or after you quantify the number of angels that can dance on the head of a pin?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well after. The number of angels that can dance on the head of a pin is 0. Because angels can't dance.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/900909-have-you-ever-used-the-werewolf-trinity-in-your-mage-game?p=905329#post905329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can't seal a spirit into a physical object with Spirit 2, you need Spirit 4 for that.<br /> With 2 you can only increase the local Gauntlet, and trap spirits within it, but it isn't an invulnerable seal (anything that can pierce the Gauntlet can pierce your trap, as it's made with the Gauntlet itself).<br /> <br /> And you always forget the most important part, the difficulty:<br /> <br /> The entrapping of a spirit needs a number of successes appropiate for the power of the Spirit. This depends, partly, on the judgement of the Storyteller, but you shouldn't assume that entrapping an Incarna will be easier than impossible (I wouldn't allow it with less than 100 successes, being very generous. All the Council of Nine was needed to entrap a single Incarna in the foundation of Horizon, it's not easy).<br /> As you can see, the system bends arround these &quot;perceived issues&quot; quite easily. Once again, I need to remember to you that magick it's deffined by its difficulty, not only by the Spheres, and entrapping an Incarna it's easily &gt;= &quot;Godlike Feat&quot;<br /> <br /> Plus, you may not know this but, in Mage, powerful spirits have Mage Spheres as a representation of their vast and all encompassing power. This it's a rule that existed from the first edition to the last. Since Lord Steel hasn't character sheet, what makes you think that he shouldn't have &quot;Spheres&quot;?. Since in werewolf these spirits can do &quot;anything within their purview&quot;, it seems appropiate that they can use open ended powers affectin all layers of reality within the conjceptual domain of the spirit. Meaning that the spirit can probably release itself or merely counter your powers with his own Dynamic Magick(tm).<br /> <br /> And that's without even entering in &quot;Storyteller's Fiat Realm&quot;. And Incarnae live in that Realm, ask any Mage book about Spirits, from the Book of Madness to M20.They all will say the same: These entities can't be faced directly.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's if you want to create a fetish. I am talking about simply creating a mirrored ball surrounding him. As described in the specific ritual which enacts his destruction, which is only difficult because Garou have to actually fight him, overpower him, and then smash the mask, and shove him into a mirrored box. The hard way. For a mage, that's a clever combination of ritual magic.<br /> <br /> This is something that's difficult only because the Garou have to actually fight their way there. With all the materials for the ritual. Past an army of Fomori.<br /> <br /> A mage needn't go through that.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T11:12:40-07:00","id":906567,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/900909-have-you-ever-used-the-werewolf-trinity-in-your-mage-game?p=906539#post906539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Assuming of course that for whatever reasons, the crossover ends up with neatly arranged sides of equivalent power.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're far past neck-deep in a situation where both games are basically tearing themselves apart. It won't be a neat and equal power that you're facing; you'll be back to being an underdog again, because you're knocking on the door that's next to what is in Mage a Caul. Nephandi <i>and</i> BSDs will be your foes, not just one or the other. The only circumstances when you can get an asymmetric advantage are at the outset of a planned crossover, when things are just heating up, or if your crossovers are very rare. With this much exposure, butting heads against a being that could basically just kill you without making any rolls at all, you won't have any advantages; notes will have been compared, and many Nephandi will be waiting in the wings, guaranteed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> When there's no reason for this to occur, because Werewolves are kind of at best inept luddites, and at worst hidebound sociopathic morons who ruin almost everything they are tasked with... </div> </div> </div>They were tasked with killing other monsters. They did this quite well for tens of thousands of years before it ran into a terrible problem. How long did it take for hubris to get the better of mages, again? Barely a few millennia?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T11:37:25-07:00","id":906589,"title":"","content":"Nephandi! Yes Terrifying. Those guys that are always there like boogeymen but get about as much done as suicide bombers. Wooh. Random spooky attack here and there.<br /> <br /> And black spiral dancers those things that won't be anywhere near you when you enact the ritual from the other side of the universe from a subdimension that doesn't technically exist in any way they're able to detect. And you could just erect a correspondence ban that prevents them from coming within a mile of you even if they could.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T13:09:24-07:00","id":906661,"title":"","content":"I grant you that I wasn't aware Lord Steel was SO weak to mirrors (I assume that this isn't a Werewolf Ritual, but a mundane action that any human would be able to do, with the right, mundane, tools. Otherwise you couldn't assume that a mage would be able to do it)<br /> But how are you going to break the mask without dealing with Steel's magical power?. Powerful spirits have the equivalent of True Magick worth of reality warping. They can do anything a mage could do. In the Old Book of Madness, you had an Incarna depicted to have all the Spheres at 5 (this included Correspondence) and Arete 10, in one of his avatars, his true form was supposed to be even more powerful than that. Don't know why you assume that Steel will be weaker or less capable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 06-03-2016, 04:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T14:10:25-07:00","id":906700,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/900909-have-you-ever-used-the-werewolf-trinity-in-your-mage-game?p=906589#post906589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nephandi! Yes Terrifying. Those guys that are always there like boogeymen but get about as much done as suicide bombers. Wooh. Random spooky attack here and there.<br /> <br /> And black spiral dancers those things that won't be anywhere near you when you enact the ritual from the other side of the universe from a subdimension that doesn't technically exist in any way they're able to detect. And you could just erect a correspondence ban that prevents them from coming within a mile of you even if they could.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not that I am a big proponent of it, but, as of Mage20, Nephandi created and largely run the Technocracy. The Technocracy largely created the World-As-We-Know-It. So, from your &quot;omnipotence of low levels of Sphere Magic&quot; POV, the Nephandi are more like a functional hands-on Illuminati. Whether they work for or with such an Incarnae, they are an asset that absolutely trumps any feeble attempts of some low-level Traditions mages, since any Conditioned Technocrats wouldn't be allowed within a mile of making such plans against associates of the highest and mightiest Technocrats of all. Hell,s the wouldn't even know there were something in the universe that might entail even thinking about plans such as these. Or even high level Traditions mages, for that matter, since they haven't been able to do the same to Control, the Antediluvians, the Neverborn, etc. even with the creation of specifically contoured sub-dimensions built for the purposes of Maeljin destruction. One of the reasons why it's pretty much a lock that it's not as easy as you are making it is that it hasn't been done. <br /> <br /> And there are Nephandi that directly serve the Wyrm. They need to be factored in as well. They may not be as organized as any Technephandi allies, but they would be adding their oomph to whatever the BSD's are doing. And they would definitely have the same powers. Like, say, Time 2, to know that they needed to have Correspondence 2 wards up to deflect the whole nonsense from happening.<br /> <br /> All that's BEFORE we start talking about the powers, abilities and innate countermagic of the entity in question.<br /> <br /> Versatility and raw power aren't the same thing. In fact, it seems like the mages might have to deal with the big bad in EXACTLY the same way the werewolves would in a FtF out and out fight because the way he has to die is EXACTLY the procedure outlined. No mystic substitutions allowed. It's written in Fate and would take significant Entropy (+ whatever else) to undo.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T17:45:17-07:00","id":906841,"title":"","content":"Except that's complete nonsense, and one of the prime reasons I don't intend to invest in Mage20. Because the Technocracy totally has the resources to destroy the world if they wanted to. It's just... honestly not a good idea at all. From a writing standpoint.<br /> <br /> And quite frankly, that's silly. So far as I'm aware, most of those things aren't actually on the Mage radar. Mages neither know about nor care about Antediluvians. At least not until one came a knocking during the week of nightmares. (That's also silly. But whatever. It's a thin line keeping mage from spilling over onto everything else.)<br /> <br /> The exact procedure is just 'break the mask to expose his face, then force him to look at his own reflection for a month.' At which point he explodes and <i>racism vanishes.</i> Because Werewolf is written as a top down world. Where you have giant gods that govern huge swathes of reality. And Mage is written from the bottom up. Where there is no fate, nor even world, except what mankind makes of it.<br /> <br /> One is about furry deathmachines desperately trying to repair a metaphorical plane in a deathspiral. Where every toxic waste dump or overpass is one more nail in the worlds coffin. There is no changing what is. Only hopefully restoring what once was and even that is an epic feat that ends up risking the end of the world.<br /> <br /> The other is about normal people discovering that the world is nothing but what they make of it. That they truly can change it. And the ludicrous levels of power that realization gives them. And the politics between factions of such people. They all want a perfect world. But what is the perfect world? There's no gods. Only men and women given godlike power and left to decide what to do with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-04T04:18:57-07:00","id":907056,"title":"","content":"<br /> If a Maeljin Incarna dies, what impedes the Urge Wyrm to just fart another one?. They didn't seem so hard to replace in the Book of the Wyrm. Almost like they weren't such big shoots. Or it's Steel so cursed that he can't possibly be recreated or replaced were to be destroyed by this mean?.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The exact procedure is just 'break the mask to expose his face, then force him to look at his own reflection for a month.' </div> </div> </div><i>A fucking month</i>. And how exactly are you going keep him that much time without him being released by other entities at some point?, do you really think that a Nephandy or some cosmic entity of near unlimited power can't just reach a Horizon Realm? (Steel looses all of his power while lookig his reflection?, because otherwise this course of action seems so doomed that it doesn't have any sense)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There's no gods. Only men and women given godlike power and left to decide what to do with it. </div> </div> </div>That's just a theory. False, if we go by the spirit hierarchy, or the theory of the Pure Ones that was there in the first/second editions. But if you swear by Revised, then consider this: You can't vanish racism, because racism it's supported by the Consensus, and thus another spirit of racism will appear if you kill the current one. Pure revised metaphysics.<br /> <br /> Plus, Mage fully addresses godlike entities, and you seem to be completely oblivious of such addressing. Because if you werent you would know that they aren't defenselss against magick.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 06-04-2016, 07:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-04T10:14:49-07:00","id":907152,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/900909-have-you-ever-used-the-werewolf-trinity-in-your-mage-game?p=906841#post906841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The other is about normal people discovering that the world is nothing but what they make of it. That they truly can change it. And the ludicrous levels of power that realization gives them. And the politics between factions of such people. They all want a perfect world. But what is the perfect world? There's no gods. Only men and women given godlike power and left to decide what to do with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a view of Mage that isn't and has never been fully supported by any version of Mage from 1st to 20th Anniversary. There are always have always been things greater than humanity and things that even a fully empowered mage cannot do. There are truths that the Consensus cannot change, no matter how many people can be convinced to believe otherwise. Barring whatever may happen after total mass Ascension. Within those bounds there is a lot of play for the masses to create inertia in one way direction or another. And the possibility to try to channel that inertia in certain directions if one is in the know about the power of belief. There is fair amount of wiggle-room on a particularized individual basis to find ways to bend and circumvent the &quot;rules&quot;, but, even then, not the &quot;base code&quot; of the Tellurian. <br /> <br /> Racism as a concept doesn't go away if you kill the big bad spirit of racism. Nor does hate. Nor does ignorance. There are other spirits in his hierarchy who will step up to take his place. Neither Werewolf or Mage is entirely top down or bottom up. As Aleph says, the Consensus doesn't stop believing such a thing as racism exists. There is probaby a momentary bubble where everyone gets a &quot;world-wide moment of clarity&quot; and racism changes just a little bit as the hierarchy struggles to or with the replacement. Mages can't get rid of it either. They can't &quot;starve&quot; the spirit of racism by uncreating it with some massive working. Even a Godlike feat of conjunctional Master level Sphere magic as a Ritual with all the assistants possible working towards the same end could do it. That's reprogramming the whole Consensus. If it were possible, it would have been done. Probably be the Union to get rid of ANY latititude for anything other than version of technomancy. At a certain point, the Ascension War is really a war for hearts and minds. Or it's &quot;leave me alone&quot; to allow me to achieve Ascension in my own way without interference.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T11:44:19-07:00","id":907767,"title":"","content":"I'm a sucker for Werewolf so I don't ignore their Cosmology, I just have it Mages are rarely wise enough to notice, but they get a rough gist of Dynamism/Stasis/Entropy are dominant spiritual Forces.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T17:02:20-07:00","id":909602,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/900909-have-you-ever-used-the-werewolf-trinity-in-your-mage-game?p=907056#post907056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a Maeljin Incarna dies, what impedes the Urge Wyrm to just fart another one?. They didn't seem so hard to replace in the Book of the Wyrm. Almost like they weren't such big shoots. Or it's Steel so cursed that he can't possibly be recreated or replaced were to be destroyed by this mean?.<br /> <br /> <br /> <i>A fucking month</i>. And how exactly are you going keep him that much time without him being released by other entities at some point?, do you really think that a Nephandy or some cosmic entity of near unlimited power can't just reach a Horizon Realm? (Steel looses all of his power while lookig his reflection?, because otherwise this course of action seems so doomed that it doesn't have any sense)<br /> <br /> <br /> That's just a theory. False, if we go by the spirit hierarchy, or the theory of the Pure Ones that was there in the first/second editions. But if you swear by Revised, then consider this: You can't vanish racism, because racism it's supported by the Consensus, and thus another spirit of racism will appear if you kill the current one. Pure revised metaphysics.<br /> <br /> Plus, Mage fully addresses godlike entities, and you seem to be completely oblivious of such addressing. Because if you werent you would know that they aren't defenselss against magick.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because? These are the rituals required to permanently destroy/seal them. As in another one DOESN'T take it's place.<br /> <br /> For example, if you just hate the current Incarnation of Lord Steel. Go stab him in the face until he dies. You become the new Maeljin of Hatred.<br /> <br /> Not a horizon realm. You take that pocket of space and knock it out of the Tellurian. Do not maintain it's links. Do not pass go. It's now effectively unfindable.<br /> <br /> And of course. That's where Mage and Werewolf Conflict. In werewolf, if you kill this guy <i>racism just goes away.</i> The worst racists are now only mildly politically incorrect. Everyone else is perfectly accepting of everyone else. In Mage, the idea of a single individual being the lynchpin to a defining personality trait for a HUGE portion of the human race is ridiculous. The idea that negative personality traits are caused by evil demons rather than just people being people is silly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/900909-have-you-ever-used-the-werewolf-trinity-in-your-mage-game?p=907152#post907152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's a view of Mage that isn't and has never been fully supported by any version of Mage from 1st to 20th Anniversary. There are always have always been things greater than humanity and things that even a fully empowered mage cannot do. There are truths that the Consensus cannot change, no matter how many people can be convinced to believe otherwise. Barring whatever may happen after total mass Ascension. Within those bounds there is a lot of play for the masses to create inertia in one way direction or another. And the possibility to try to channel that inertia in certain directions if one is in the know about the power of belief. There is fair amount of wiggle-room on a particularized individual basis to find ways to bend and circumvent the &quot;rules&quot;, but, even then, not the &quot;base code&quot; of the Tellurian.<br /> <br /> Racism as a concept doesn't go away if you kill the big bad spirit of racism. Nor does hate. Nor does ignorance. There are other spirits in his hierarchy who will step up to take his place. Neither Werewolf or Mage is entirely top down or bottom up. As Aleph says, the Consensus doesn't stop believing such a thing as racism exists. There is probaby a momentary bubble where everyone gets a &quot;world-wide moment of clarity&quot; and racism changes just a little bit as the hierarchy struggles to or with the replacement. Mages can't get rid of it either. They can't &quot;starve&quot; the spirit of racism by uncreating it with some massive working. Even a Godlike feat of conjunctional Master level Sphere magic as a Ritual with all the assistants possible working towards the same end could do it. That's reprogramming the whole Consensus. If it were possible, it would have been done. Probably be the Union to get rid of ANY latititude for anything other than version of technomancy. At a certain point, the Ascension War is really a war for hearts and minds. Or it's &quot;leave me alone&quot; to allow me to achieve Ascension in my own way without interference.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Are there? Or are there just things a fully empowered mage hasn't yet realized they can do?<br /> <br /> That's one of the key problems of the Technocracy. They identify certain things they think should be good. And then they exclude the possibility of all else, in order to solidify and simplify magic down to something even a sleeper can understand. Sacrificing untold possibility for common utility.<br /> <br /> The rulebook even says that you should keep to the feeling of it, rather than the rules. Given that the spheres are a recent invention, and are treated more like a useful rubric of knowledge rather than an actual concrete accurate representation of how reality works...<br /> <br /> And no. The ritual detailing lord Steeles destruction outright says all but the worst racists, homophobes, etc stop being so. And even the worst ones disposition is much improved. Permanently.<br /> <br /> And considering the union has a procedure that turns anything other than Enlightened Science vulgar, no matter how coincidental it may be elsewhere. And all enlightened science coincidental, no matter how much the sleepers disbelieve... And as a side effect also turns all non-mage supernaturals into thaumavores who require a point of quintessence every day or else they sicken and die...<br /> <br /> And yet they don't use it except rarely. For... whatever reason.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T19:47:45-07:00","id":909757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Not a horizon realm. You take that pocket of space and knock it out of the Tellurian. Do not maintain it's links. Do not pass go. It's now effectively unfindable. </div> </div> </div>&quot;Outside of the Tellurian&quot; it's a funny way to say &quot;to the Deep Umbra&quot;. Guess where's Malfeas according to Mage Cosmology: In the Deep Umbra. Not unreachable at all. Plus, if you know exactly what to search, Magick can find anything anywhere.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Are there? Or are there just things a fully empowered mage hasn't yet realized they can do? </div> </div> </div>That's something that nobody knows. It's up to the Storyteller if the world has basis appart from the human will (and Prime). Most Mage books defend the posibility of impossibilities enough so you can use them in your games.<br /> <br /> Besides, you're refusing to tackle the issue of Incarnas having powers that can rival with True Magick. Since you can't prove that they don't, you can't dissuade me of, say, saying that Steel has protected his mask with a ward that prevents it to be taken away/attacked with Corr (I would protect my mask if I know it's such a heavy weakness).<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And considering the union has a procedure that turns anything other than Enlightened Science vulgar, no matter how coincidental it may be elsewhere. And all enlightened science coincidental, no matter how much the sleepers disbelieve... And as a side effect also turns all non-mage supernaturals into thaumavores who require a point of quintessence every day or else they sicken and die...<br /> <br /> And yet they don't use it except rarely. For... whatever reason. </div> </div> </div>They don't use it because the Procedure itself it's Vulgar...and because Paradox can erode such effects, or impede to make them Permanent, or prevent you to use them in large areas. They preffer to use them in the Umbra, there, the consequences are usualy lighter.<br /> <br /> It only turns some non-mage into thaumnivores...other mysteriously resist the effect. Surely because some uncoscious nonsense that has never been proved by any Mind Master.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The rulebook even says that you should keep to the feeling of it, rather than the rules. Given that the spheres are a recent invention, and are treated more like a useful rubric of knowledge rather than an actual concrete accurate representation of how reality works... </div> </div> </div>It's funny how you interpret this as meaning that mages can do anything they want without limits, and not as, sometimes, you ain't going to be able to do what the rules state that you can do...because sometimes, &quot;the feeling of it&quot; it's that a given magick should cause a far greater Paradox than what the rules indicate (like, say, trying to overrule the Consensus with magick), or that a given spell should be very hard to do if powerful mystical influences push against it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 06-07-2016, 10:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T20:27:20-07:00","id":909784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/900909-have-you-ever-used-the-werewolf-trinity-in-your-mage-game?p=909602#post909602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Because? These are the rituals required to permanently destroy/seal them. As in another one DOESN'T take it's place.<br /> <br /> For example, if you just hate the current Incarnation of Lord Steel. Go stab him in the face until he dies. You become the new Maeljin of Hatred.<br /> <br /> Not a horizon realm. You take that pocket of space and knock it out of the Tellurian. Do not maintain it's links. Do not pass go. It's now effectively unfindable.<br /> <br /> And of course. That's where Mage and Werewolf Conflict. In werewolf, if you kill this guy <i>racism just goes away.</i> The worst racists are now only mildly politically incorrect. Everyone else is perfectly accepting of everyone else. In Mage, the idea of a single individual being the lynchpin to a defining personality trait for a HUGE portion of the human race is ridiculous. The idea that negative personality traits are caused by evil demons rather than just people being people is silly.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't go away. It is significantly reduced in intensity for a period of time ranging from one to ten years until another Maeljin takes its place. The normal workings of Incarnae are somewhat different from other spirits, as killing one only prompts a Celestine to promote another into its place. You have to kill a Celestine to actually take out a big concept, and Celestines are so huge that their avatars need avatars to speak to mortal beings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T10:24:37-07:00","id":910171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/900909-have-you-ever-used-the-werewolf-trinity-in-your-mage-game?p=909602#post909602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Because? These are the rituals required to permanently destroy/seal them. As in another one DOESN'T take it's place.<br /> <br /> For example, if you just hate the current Incarnation of Lord Steel. Go stab him in the face until he dies. You become the new Maeljin of Hatred.<br /> <br /> Not a horizon realm. You take that pocket of space and knock it out of the Tellurian. Do not maintain it's links. Do not pass go. It's now effectively unfindable.<br /> <br /> And of course. That's where Mage and Werewolf Conflict. In werewolf, if you kill this guy <i>racism just goes away.</i> The worst racists are now only mildly politically incorrect. Everyone else is perfectly accepting of everyone else. In Mage, the idea of a single individual being the lynchpin to a defining personality trait for a HUGE portion of the human race is ridiculous. The idea that negative personality traits are caused by evil demons rather than just people being people is silly.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Are there? Or are there just things a fully empowered mage hasn't yet realized they can do?<br /> <br /> That's one of the key problems of the Technocracy. They identify certain things they think should be good. And then they exclude the possibility of all else, in order to solidify and simplify magic down to something even a sleeper can understand. Sacrificing untold possibility for common utility.<br /> <br /> The rulebook even says that you should keep to the feeling of it, rather than the rules. Given that the spheres are a recent invention, and are treated more like a useful rubric of knowledge rather than an actual concrete accurate representation of how reality works...<br /> <br /> And no. The ritual detailing lord Steeles destruction outright says all but the worst racists, homophobes, etc stop being so. And even the worst ones disposition is much improved. Permanently.<br /> <br /> And considering the union has a procedure that turns anything other than Enlightened Science vulgar, no matter how coincidental it may be elsewhere. And all enlightened science coincidental, no matter how much the sleepers disbelieve... And as a side effect also turns all non-mage supernaturals into thaumavores who require a point of quintessence every day or else they sicken and die...<br /> <br /> And yet they don't use it except rarely. For... whatever reason.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. There are. Read M20 where they are explicitly set out. Which is just a compilation and organization of relevant material that has been addressed hodge-podge previously. So, yeah, since the get-go there are things that mages can't do. There are some absolutes: They can't make there not be such a thing as magic. They cannot unmake the Umbrae (though their permeability can be squishy). There are some default settings that can change, but in the absence of them changing them, there are set things. They really can't get rid of baseline up-ness and down-ness. Thsey can't &quot;unmake&quot; a status like that of &quot;vampirism&quot; or &quot;death&quot;, etc. (Sure it MAY be possible to make an indvidial werewolf or vampire here and there stop being that, maybe, but, aside from killing off all the relevant nasties, it's not a holistic phenomenon. Sure, Voormas may have tried &quot;to get rid of death&quot; but he was really just adding the state of &quot;being dead&quot; to the set of &quot;being alive&quot; by merging the edges of the Low Umbra and the Skinlands in a way consistent with their respective &quot;squishy-ness&quot;.)<br /> <br /> However or whatever sets these up, it's probably not something that can be accomplished by effective Consensus leadership for whatever reason. Perhaps the Tellurian believes in itself in a fundamental way that embraces and enfolds the Consensus of Humanity. Or whatever. But there it is.<br /> <br /> So what if you get rid of &quot;Hate&quot; from a WEREWOLF perspective? Then something else will take it's place. I don't have to HATE you to treat you like shit. I can be DISGUSTED by you. Or PITY your. Or feel DESPAIR. Or just feel enough GREED to want to take all of your stuff until you are miserable unto death. Hate as the Hate that Steel represents is gone. Other negative things will flow in around the edges. The Universe may be fractionally better for it, but that doesn't make &quot;it all better&quot;. There is a lot of negativity out there, and it doesn't really matter what the motivation is if the end result is the same.<br /> <br /> This just seems like the weirdest argument position to come from. 1. Werewolf is RIGHT. Lord Steel IS Hate and what Werewolf says about defeating him is uttery 100% right in every way. 2. Werewolf is WRONG and Mage is RIGHT because Mages have supreme power (wait, didn't Werewolf's position on the importance of Lord Steel trump EVERYTHING else... oh well....) and, since they have some apparently effective workarounds, then Mages can accomplish the nearly-impossible utterly epic in Werewolf with ease. There are some logical fallacies buried in changing perspectives to armor your arguments against all comers.<br /> <br /> If you want mages to be this omnipotent, effectively from Arete 2 on, that's your call. It's your game. Golden Rule, etc. etc. To my mind, and probably to most, it's not a very interesting game. When characters have unlimited power and there is effectively no opposition to their level of creative bullshit as permitted by their ST, it's just creative mental masturbation and will almost certainly end up full of sound and fury, but, ultimately, signify nothing.<br /> <br /> As for the Spheres and whether they are an &quot;in game thing&quot; or a reflection of the underlying &quot;laws of how things work&quot;.... well that's been argued and hashed and rehashed in post after post. It's an open question. But, to my mind, it definitely seems more like it's the later than the former, particularly in how the game is set up. (With everyone using them, including Orphans who don't know ANYTHING about some agreement between some weird dudes several centuries ago...) It's not just how Mages think about things affecting how they do things, it's a reflection of how they do things reflecting the way things are (now.... not that they always were thus.... )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1062,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","user":"Ajax","date":". 06-09-2016, 07:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-03T12:54:39-07:00","id":1302307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/900909-have-you-ever-used-the-werewolf-trinity-in-your-mage-game?p=902372#post902372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">rit world more than Mages, but they are actually quite weak on major metaphysical philosophies. Attributing all their problems to the Wyrm is simply their way of dealing with the Problem of Evil.<br /> <br /> The game was originally written with the intent that all of them crossovered to one another. That quickly fell apart as 1) there were not enough common mechanics to make it work, 2) as each line developed, little bits of inconsistent canon were introduced especially as the first games had many more supplements published before some of the game lines had even begun, and 3) the various line developers became very protective of their own line and couldn't work well with others to tell a single setting. There were too many ideas (and egos) that worked against each other. So before too long, the line changed from crossover is great and allowed, to none of the games crossover and canon in one game shouldn't be taken into the next line. That way each developer could do whatever they liked and ignore what another developer was doing. Well, it is at least one way of dealing with office politics.</div> </div> </div> </div>I swear, I almost thought you were talking about the Traditions and not the World of Darkness game lines.<br /> <br /> Oh wait...<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13189-knowledgeseeker","name":"Knowledgeseeker","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T17:20:01-07:00","id":1307063,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Please don't necro threads to pick a fight with a 